Z||000003||tgowens||11-22-2000||01:51 AM||||here is the one I use and the ones that we sell at the shop........ <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gmplayer_1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>                  <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                              <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> - Classic Fiero Owners Group<BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.net/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroshop.net/</A> - Fiero Shop - Richmond, CA - 1-510-23-FIERO||||reg||1
Z||000004||sparks||11-22-2000||08:48 AM||||I'm pretty happy with my Aiwa car stereos.<P>I've got one in my 97 Wrangler and another in my Fiero.<P>Like it was mentioned the display can be hard to read during the day.  Direct sunlight is easy to read, but if there's a glare on the display it's difficult to read.<P>They sound great to me.<BR><P>------------------<BR><BR>Adam Sparks||||reg||1
Z||000005||deceler8||11-22-2000||10:46 AM||||Had an Aiwa in my last car...a fantastic radio and great audio quality, but the red LCD display was impossible to read in the daytime.<P>Really frustrating...<P>In fact, it got stolen and I was glad it was gone. Just went back to the factory radio.<P>In all the cars I've owned, no factory radio has performed as well as the one in my Fiero. Which is surprising, since Delco radios used to have a reputation for being underpowered.||||reg||1
Z||000006||TheFiero64||11-22-2000||11:53 AM||||I like the one I have the best. It looks like it was put there in the factory. I get a lot of double takes <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. It even lights up red. It has never skipped. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CDrad.JPG"> <P>------------------<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||sparks||11-22-2000||12:47 PM||||I would've liked to had a later factory Pontiac CD player for the Fiero but I couldn't justify the price.  By the time I bought the adaptor kit and the radio etc. it cost me under $60, the radio was on clearance due to be discontinued.<P>Compared to $300+ for a nice Delco CD player...<P>Still, maybe someday when I've got the Fiero the way I want it mechanically...<P>------------------<BR><BR>Adam Sparks||||reg||1
